# MD5 Password Cracking Challenge Report

## Overview

This project demonstrates an offline password cracking attack against weak MD5 password hashes using Hashcat and common password wordlists. The challenge simulates a real-world scenario where a web application stores user passwords using insecure hashing algorithms without proper salting or modern cryptographic protections.

The objective was to:

* Crack MD5 password hashes
* Understand dictionary-based password attacks
* Learn Hashcat workflows
* Analyze weak credential storage risks
* Understand OWASP cryptographic failures
* Document findings and remediation guidance

