# Technical Analysis

## Why MD5 Is Insecure

MD5 is considered cryptographically broken because:

* Extremely fast hashing speed
* No adaptive cost factor
* Vulnerable to GPU acceleration
* Susceptible to rainbow table attacks
* No built-in salting
* Deprecated for password storage

Attackers can test millions or billions of password guesses per second.

