# Conclusion

The exercise successfully demonstrated how weak password hashing implementations using MD5 can be exploited through offline cracking attacks.

A total of 108 password hashes were recovered using a standard dictionary attack against a large common-password wordlist.

The findings reinforce the importance of:

* Secure password hashing
* Modern cryptographic standards
* Strong password policies
* Defense-in-depth security controls
* Regular security assessments

Organizations using MD5 for password storage remain highly vulnerable to credential compromise and account takeover attacks.

